menu "Standalone captions streaming"
config CAPTIONS_STREAM_METRICS
    bool "Collect bounded streaming lock and capture diagnostics"
    default n
    help
        Adds operation timing, memory-traffic counters and I2S loss counters.
        Use the USB command perf dump between test inputs. Results are emitted
        outside the streaming lock. This changes timing and needs overhead controls.
config CAPTIONS_CAPTURE_FEATURES
    bool "Compute reusable features during capture"
    default y
config CAPTIONS_OVERLAP_GATE
    bool "Emit an overlap flag per final caption (also needs -DHW1_OVERLAP_GATE=ON)"
    default n
    help
        Runs the small overlap-gate model on the segment's raw log-mel rows after
        the caption is emitted and publishes an "overlap" event beside the speaker
        label. Caption text is unchanged. Needs /sd/STT Models/overlap_gate.espdl;
        without it the gate is absent and nothing is emitted.
config CAPTIONS_CLEAR_COMMITTED_FEATURES
    bool "Clear only committed feature-cache rows (experimental)"
    depends on CAPTIONS_CAPTURE_FEATURES
    default n
    help
        Preserve initial whole-pool clearing, then clear the complete written
        prefix on retirement. Reader pins and generation checks remain intact.
        Requires the capture-lock qualification described in the project plan.
config CAPTIONS_DRAFTS
    bool "Publish preemptible live drafts"
    default y
config CAPTIONS_X2F_DRAFT_PACING
    bool "Use x2 compute-paced drafts with a fast first draft (experimental)"
    depends on CAPTIONS_DRAFTS
    default n
    help
        Keep a one-second audio floor for the first preview, then require
        at least 600 ms of new audio or twice the previous draft compute time.
        A new phrase does not inherit a slow previous phrase's draft delay.
        Requires standalone device latency/accuracy qualification.
config CAPTIONS_DECISION_PRE_EMPHASIS
    bool "Level-robust phrase onset (pre-emphasised decision, room-matched)"
    default y
    help
        Phrases may also open and stay open on the level of the pre-emphasised
        signal x[n] - 0.97 x[n-1], scaled to the room's ambient by a gain the
        segmenter re-learns on every idle frame (150 percent). This matches the
        spectral tilt between room tone and speech, so far or quiet speech whose
        raw level sits at the fixed 45-count floor is found; the 45/16 floors
        still bound it, so speech a few dB quieter again is missed. Only the
        segmentation decision changes: the audio given to the recognizer is
        unchanged. Host replay of P4 bench recordings (deployed model +
        meeting.lm): WER 74.58 -> 52.50 % and 71.25 -> 45.21 % on the far
        recordings (56.67 -> 43.44 % on one taken at PDM x8 / 120 Hz),
        28.35 -> 26.79 % on the noise playlist, 20.64 -> 21.18 % up close.
        It opens more and longer segments on background speech and noise
        (noise playlist: 32 -> 184 s of 190 s inside phrases, false words on
        noise 4 -> 8, in 2 -> 4 segments) and sends 2.2-2.7x the audio to
        the recognizer.
        Not qualified on the device.
        Choose n (or add sdkconfig.prev_onset) to restore the previous detector
        exactly, e.g. to reproduce device results recorded before 12 Nov 2026.
config CAPTIONS_DECISION_MODULATION_GATE
    bool "Level-robust onset: noisy-room mode (modulation gate, raw-latch hold)"
    depends on CAPTIONS_DECISION_PRE_EMPHASIS
    default n
    help
        Noisy-room mode: trades far and quiet speech for less noise inside
        phrases. The pre-emphasised level may open or hold a phrase only while
        its last 500 ms is modulated (90th percentile frame level above 3.0 x
        the 10th), so steady fans and hiss leave the raw rule in charge; and a
        phrase that only the pre-emphasised level opened is held open by that
        level alone until the raw level reaches the raw onset rule by itself.
        Host replay of the P4 bench recordings (deployed model + meeting.lm):
        noise inside phrases 31-46 s -> 3-9 s per day recording and 184 -> 66 s
        on the noise playlist, but WER 52.50 -> 61.25 %, 45.21 -> 46.56 % and
        43.44 -> 44.79 % on the three day recordings scored, with no fewer
        false words on noise; steady night babble is not reduced at all, and
        a talker under bursty noise loses 14-21 s more speech. Not qualified
        on the device. Off (n) keeps the onset above bit-for-bit.
config CAPTIONS_TRIM_SILENCE
    bool "Retain 500 ms of trailing silence (requires audio qualification)"
    default n
config CAPTIONS_SPECULATIVE_FINAL
    bool "Compute exact speculative finals before segment closure"
    depends on CAPTIONS_TRIM_SILENCE
    default y
endmenu
